<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Madison is a 23-year-old man with functional/dissociative seizures, depression, and anxiety, on sertraline 50 mg, who called this morning and was seen the same day. Since yesterday morning he has vomited six times and had loose watery stools about eight times, with cramping; two people in the house where he had dinner two days ago have the same illness. He has kept down small sips of water since last night. He has had a temperature of 37.8 C, no blood in his stool, no severe or constant abdominal pain, and no recent travel or antibiotics. He vomited his sertraline yesterday and did not take today&apos;s dose. Last evening, while lying on the bathroom floor feeling faint and wretched, he had a typical functional seizure lasting about three minutes; there was no tongue biting, and he recognized the warning feeling but could not stop it. He has had no thoughts of death or self-harm. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Yesterday morning; household contacts with the same illness</td></tr><tr><td>Fluids</td><td>Small sips of water kept down since last night</td></tr><tr><td>Event</td><td>One typical functional seizure last evening, about three minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Sertraline 50 mg; yesterday&apos;s dose vomited, today&apos;s not taken</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>No suicidal thoughts</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

